repo: kagent-dev/kagent (upstream), plus fork additions applied by hand
commit: 61b153c18bfe4c8cb7ffa54ddcc352c417e3c801
paths: proto/kagent/api/v1/{common.proto,runtime.proto,sessions.proto,agents.proto,scheduled_runs.proto,checkpoints.proto}
notes: |
  PROVISIONAL. The commit above is upstream kagent-dev/kagent main, the base of the fork branch
  oldsj/kagent mainloop-substrate-1-0, which had no fork commits when this was vendored. The six
  files are upstream's at that commit with the fork additions the port keeps re-applied by hand,
  at their v1alpha1 field numbers:
    common.proto     message Workspace
    sessions.proto   rpc PrepareSessionWorkspace; Session fields 16-22; CreateSessionRequest
                     fields 6-8; messages RuntimeAssociation, SecretKeyReference, SessionCredential,
                     DevelopmentEnvironment, RuntimeComposition, PrepareSessionWorkspace{Request,
                     Response}, WorkspacePreparationReceipt
    checkpoints.proto ForkSessionRequest.fresh_conversation = 3
  Once the fork branch carries these, copy the files verbatim from it, set repo to oldsj/kagent and
  the commit to the revision infra deploys, and update deployedSourceRevision in source_test.go.

  Go and Connect clients are generated from these by `go generate ./...`, driven by
  server/tools/kagentproto (protocompile + protoc-gen-go + protoc-gen-connect-go; no
  buf CLI, since buf.yaml's module deps need BSR access this tree does not have).

  To refresh by hand from a fork checkout:
    commit=<new commit>
    fork=~/dev/kagent   # or wherever the oldsj/kagent fork is checked out
    dest=server/third_party/kagentproto/kagent/api/v1
    for f in common runtime sessions agents scheduled_runs checkpoints; do
      git -C "$fork" show "$commit:proto/kagent/api/v1/$f.proto" >"$dest/$f.proto"
    done
  then update the commit above and run `go generate ./...` from server/.
